{{!
    Consent Manager override of java-micronaut/server/controller.mustache.

    The stock template derives a routed method's parameters from the operation's
    parameters and request body alone, and annotates every one of them with a
    binding annotation. This service needs one more: the caller, as a typed
    ConsentManagerPrincipal. PrincipalResolutionFilter resolves a principal only
    for a route that declares such a parameter, and PrincipalArgumentBinder is a
    TypedRequestArgumentBinder, so the parameter has to sit on the *routed*
    method and carry no binding annotation - neither of which the stock template
    can produce.

    An operation therefore opts in with `x-principal: <simple class name>`, and
    that parameter is emitted first, fully qualified so no import is needed.
    SpecSecurityConsistencyTest fails any secured operation that omits it.

    Everything else is the stock template verbatim; partials still resolve
    against the generator's embedded templates.
}}
